{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These are the proverbs of Solomon son of David, king of Israel,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for gaining wisdom and discipline, for comprehending words of insight,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "and for receiving instruction in wise living and in righteousness, justice, and equity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To impart prudence to the simple and knowledge and discretion to the young,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "let the wise listen and gain instruction, and the discerning acquire wise counsel",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "by understanding the proverbs and parables, the sayings and riddles of the wise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge, but fools despise wisdom and discipline.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Listen, my son, to your father’s instruction, and do not forsake the teaching of your mother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they are a garland of grace on your head and a pendant around your neck.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, if sinners entice you, do not yield to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If they say, “Come along, let us lie in wait for blood, let us ambush the innocent without cause,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "let us swallow them alive like Sheol, and whole like those descending into the Pit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We will find all manner of precious goods; we will fill our houses with plunder.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Throw in your lot with us; let us all share one purse” —",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "my son, do not walk the road with them or set foot upon their path.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For their feet run to evil, and they are swift to shed blood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How futile it is to spread the net where any bird can see it!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they lie in wait for their own blood; they ambush their own lives.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Such is the fate of all who are greedy, whose unjust gain takes the lives of its possessors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wisdom calls out in the street, she lifts her voice in the square;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "in the main concourse she cries aloud, at the city gates she makes her speech:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "“How long, O simple ones, will you love your simple ways? How long will scoffers delight in their scorn and fools hate knowledge?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If you had repented at my rebuke, then surely I would have poured out my spirit on you; I would have made my words known to you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because you refused my call, and no one took my outstretched hand,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "because you neglected all my counsel, and wanted none of my correction,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "in turn I will mock your calamity; I will sneer when terror strikes you,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "when your dread comes like a storm, and your destruction like a whirlwind, when distress and anguish overwhelm you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they will call on me, but I will not answer; they will earnestly seek me, but will not find me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they hated knowledge and chose not to fear the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They accepted none of my counsel; they despised all my reproof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So they will eat the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own devices.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the waywardness of the simple will slay them, and the complacency of fools will destroy them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.1.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.1.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But whoever listens to me will dwell in safety, secure from the fear of evil.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
